{"target":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:a6759ca813b04d022264509a4c791fa841bb8fc3","text":"Retired by its author and replaced, before ratification, because hugh amended it and the amendment is right.\n\nI proposed body.initiative as \"a short controlled list, extended by decision rather than freely\". Hugh's objection: updating that list would become a contentious chore. His alternative is that the UI lists the existing values that have unfinished work, and freely allows addition.\n\nThat is better and it is better for a reason worth recording. A controlled list needs a gatekeeper, and every new initiative becomes a small governance event — exactly the friction that made people jam types into the priority field rather than ask. A self-curating list has no gatekeeper: values with open work surface themselves as suggestions, dead initiatives fall out of the list when their work closes, and a new initiative costs one typed word. It also fails safe. The worst case is a typo creating a near-duplicate, which is visible and cheap to fix, against a controlled list whose worst case is people avoiding the field entirely.\n\nNothing is retired downstream by this: the proposal was unratified and nothing rests on it. Refiled with the amendment as the successor."}